[Example Rules]
Rule 32 (Integer indices only valid with int-compatible dtype)
{v_1 : tuple(int), v_2 : dtype} |= ∀i ∈ [0, v_1.len - 1] : v_1[i] ≥ 0 ∧ v_2 = 1 ∨ v_2 = 2 ∨ v_2 = 3 ∨ v_2 = 4 ∨ v_2 = 5

Rule 5 (index tensor (v_2) should be within the range of input tensor)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= min(v_2) ≥ 0 ∧ ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) − 1] : max(v_2) ≤ shape(v_1, i) − 1

Rule 26 (tuple of ints used as kernel size must have length 2)
{v_1 : tuple(int)} |= v_1.len = 2 ∧ ∀i ∈ [0, 1] : v_1[i] > 0

Rule 2 (v_2 should be a valid dimension of input tensor)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : int} |= −1 × ndim(v_1) ≤ v_2 ∧ v_2 ≤ ndim(v_1) − 1

Rule 10 (valid 2D transposed convolution)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor, v_3 : int, v_4 : int} |= ndim(v_1) = 4 ∧ ndim(v_2) = 4 ∧ v_3 ≥ 1 ∧ v_4 ≥ 0 ∧ v_3 × (shape(v_1, 2) − 1) + shape(v_2, 2) − 2 × v_4 > 0 ∧ v_3 × (shape(v_1, 3) − 1) + shape(v_2, 3) − 2 × v_4 > 0

